## uc--evaluate-ground-truth--setup

Orchestrator. Pulls server-filtered diffing rows; writes a working file inside the run folder; fans out per-question sub-agents.

### Preconditions (fail-fast)
- `bun dev` must be running on `localhost:3000`. If not, STOP. User must start it.
- `data/<uc>/runs/<run>/gt-eval.json` must NOT exist. If it does, STOP — eval already in progress.

### Steps
- `GET /api/uc/<uc>/runs/<run>/gt-eval-candidates` → `GroundTruthEvalCandidate[]`
  - server filters: ≥1 competitor `answer.verdict ∈ {wrong, partial}`
  - all competitor answers for those questions included (context for the evaluator)
- write the response to `data/<uc>/runs/<run>/gt-eval.json` (committed; audit trail)
- chunk + spawn ≤10 sub-agents in parallel (Agent tool, `subagent_type: general-purpose`)
  - each sub-agent invokes `uc--evaluate-ground-truth--question` per `questionId` in its batch
- merge sub-agent results back into `gt-eval.json` (attach `subAgentVerdict` per entry)
- present `gt-wrong` set + proposed answers; on approval, apply via `uc--edit-structure`
- never auto-rewrite `structure.json`

